@page "/"

<PageTitle>Alfa | Modern Security Orchestration</PageTitle>

<div class="landing-shell">
    <section class="landing-hero">
        <div class="hero-copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Enterprise policy orchestration</span>
            <h1>Deploy, enforce, and audit security policies from one premium command center.</h1>
            <p>Alfa combines a hardened C++ enforcement core, an intuitive .NET dashboard, and a polished CLI so teams can manage endpoint protection with confidence.</p>
            <div class="cta-group">
                <a class="primary-button" href="/dashboard">Open dashboard</a>
                <a class="secondary-button" href="/rules">Explore rules</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-statistics">
            <div class="stat-panel accent">
                <strong>99.9%</strong>
                <span>Policy delivery consistency</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-panel">
                <strong>4.3ms</strong>
                <span>Average local rule evaluation</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-panel accent-secondary">
                <strong>Real-time</strong>
                <span>Always-on telemetry streaming</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-features">
        <article class="feature-card">
            <h2>Unified security operations</h2>
            <p>Manage rules, telemetry, and devices in a single, responsive control plane designed for lean security teams.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
            <h2>Hardened local enforcement</h2>
            <p>Secure command delivery and local policy execution are protected by HMAC signatures and immutable state persistence.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
            <h2>Enterprise-ready workflows</h2>
            <p>Use the web console or CLI to deploy updates, validate compliance, and review audit trails without leaving the platform.</p>
        </article>
    </section>
</div>
